WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome. This class treats agent
operations as a system discipline,

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
not as prompt editing. We will classify
evidence across eight

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
boundaries, contain ongoing impact,
reconcile uncertain actions, recover

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
within tested limits, communicate what is
known, and convert the

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
incident into regression tests and
controls. The incident and lab

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
are fictional and deterministic. No live
model, provider, notification service,

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
transfer system, or approval system will
be contacted during this

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
lesson.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.286
Begin with the failed boundary, and do not
confuse a

10
00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:40.571
fluent sentence with a complete diagnosis.
A model failure is

11
00:00:40.571 --> 00:00:44.857
unsupported or incorrect generation. A
prompt failure is ambiguous, conflicting,

12
00:00:44.857 --> 00:00:49.143
or incomplete instruction. A tool failure
can involve a bad

13
00:00:49.143 --> 00:00:53.429
contract, authorization, execution, or
postcondition. Retrieval fails when the

14
00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:57.714
needed source is missing or stale. Data
fails when records

15
00:00:57.714 --> 00:01:02.000
are malformed, poisoned, incorrectly
scoped, or cross-tenant. Policy can permit

16
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.286
a forbidden action or block an escalation
that is required.

17
00:01:06.286 --> 00:01:10.571
Orchestration can misroute work, loop,
race, retry unsafely, or lose

18
00:01:10.571 --> 00:01:14.857
state. Infrastructure includes capacity,
network, dependencies, credentials,

19
00:01:14.857 --> 00:01:19.143
storage, and deployment. These are
diagnostic locations, not blame labels.

20
00:01:19.143 --> 00:01:23.429
One incident can contain several classes.
Record the observed evidence,

21
00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:27.714
the boundary it supports, and what remains
unknown. In our

22
00:01:27.714 --> 00:01:32.000
incident, the sentence all actions
completed is model evidence. The

23
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.286
obsolete policy is retrieval and data
evidence. The blind retry

24
00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:40.571
is orchestration evidence. The timeout is
infrastructure evidence, but it

25
00:01:40.571 --> 00:01:44.857
does not tell us whether the write
committed. Therefore, changing

26
00:01:44.857 --> 00:01:49.143
the model alone would not repair this
incident. A useful

27
00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:53.429
first record has three columns: symptom,
supported boundary, and evidence

28
00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:57.714
still needed. That discipline prevents a
convenient but unsupported root-cause

29
00:01:57.714 --> 00:02:02.000
claim.

30
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.429
Triage asks what may have been affected
and whether harm

31
00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:10.857
can continue. Assess users, tenants, data,
permissions, external actions, money,

32
00:02:10.857 --> 00:02:15.286
availability, legal duties, safety duties,
and active automation. Severity follows

33
00:02:15.286 --> 00:02:19.714
actual and credible potential impact, not
the fluency of the

34
00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:24.143
agent and not the familiarity of an error
message. Containment

35
00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:28.571
comes before a long explanation when
unsafe behavior may continue.

36
00:02:28.571 --> 00:02:33.000
Possible controls include pausing one
workflow or tool, revoking credentials,

37
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.429
disabling a route, reducing concurrency,
stopping retries, using a safe

38
00:02:37.429 --> 00:02:41.857
read-only fallback, or requiring manual
approval. Choose the narrowest control

39
00:02:41.857 --> 00:02:46.286
that stops credible harm. Preserve
secret-safe traces, configuration

40
00:02:46.286 --> 00:02:50.714
versions, request and operation
identifiers, retrieved-document versions,

41
00:02:50.714 --> 00:02:55.143
idempotency keys, and postcondition
evidence before mutable state changes. In

42
00:02:55.143 --> 00:02:59.571
the fictional incident, the transfer tool
is paused at 09:04

43
00:02:59.571 --> 00:03:04.000
UTC. Automated retries are disabled at
09:05. The audit tool

44
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.429
remains available only through a bounded
recovery command. This is

45
00:03:08.429 --> 00:03:12.857
narrower than shutting down every service,
and safer than allowing

46
00:03:12.857 --> 00:03:17.286
the agent to continue. A containment
record must say what

47
00:03:17.286 --> 00:03:21.714
stopped, what remains available, who can
authorize recovery, how the

48
00:03:21.714 --> 00:03:26.143
original evidence is preserved, and how
the control will be

49
00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:30.571
validated. NIST connects impact analysis,
containment, recovery, and lessons

50
00:03:30.571 --> 00:03:35.000
learned. They are parts of one response,
not unrelated tickets.

51
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.487
Now work the complete dossier. At 09:00
UTC, fictional incident

52
00:03:39.487 --> 00:03:43.974
INC-2042 begins when tenant-a asks an
agent to apply a

53
00:03:43.974 --> 00:03:48.462
reserve policy and record the decision.
Retrieval returns policy version

54
00:03:48.462 --> 00:03:52.949
2025-01, although version 2026-04 is
required. At 09:01, transfer-100 sends

55
00:03:52.949 --> 00:03:57.436
100 fixture units from operating to
reserve under idempotency key

56
00:03:57.436 --> 00:04:01.923
pay-100. The transport times out after the
write reaches the

57
00:04:01.923 --> 00:04:06.410
tool. The ledger nevertheless contains
confirmed entry L-1. Starting balances

58
00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.897
were operating 1000 and reserve 0. The
persisted balances are

59
00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:15.385
operating 900 and reserve 100. At 09:02,
audit-7 times out

60
00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:19.872
before any ledger entry is created. At
09:03, notice-9 has

61
00:04:19.872 --> 00:04:24.359
a persisted pending record, so its
external postcondition cannot be

62
00:04:24.359 --> 00:04:28.846
verified. At that same time, the agent
says all actions

63
00:04:28.846 --> 00:04:33.333
completed. At 09:04, the responder
declares SEV-1 because a consequential

64
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:37.821
transfer used stale governing evidence and
another external action remains

65
00:04:37.821 --> 00:04:42.308
uncertain. At 09:05, retries are disabled.
Reconciliation begins at 09:08.

66
00:04:42.308 --> 00:04:46.795
At 09:14, authorized compensation restores
the balances. At 09:16, the

67
00:04:46.795 --> 00:04:51.282
missing audit write is retried once with
its original idempotency

68
00:04:51.282 --> 00:04:55.769
key. At 09:18, the pending notification is
escalated without retry.

69
00:04:55.769 --> 00:05:00.256
At 09:24, validation and handoff complete.
The elapsed response time

70
00:05:00.256 --> 00:05:04.744
is 24 minutes, because 09:24 minus 09:00
equals 24 minutes.

71
00:05:04.744 --> 00:05:09.231
The matrix now reads: model, unsupported
completion claim; prompt, completion

72
00:05:09.231 --> 00:05:13.718
was allowed without postcondition
evidence; tool, transfer response timed

73
00:05:13.718 --> 00:05:18.205
out and notification confirmation was not
exposed; retrieval, obsolete policy

74
00:05:18.205 --> 00:05:22.692
selected; data, stale policy entered the
decision context; policy, a

75
00:05:22.692 --> 00:05:27.179
consequential action proceeded under an
obsolete rule and compensation needs

76
00:05:27.179 --> 00:05:31.667
separate authorization; orchestration,
timeout was treated as retryable;

77
00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:36.154
infrastructure, transport timeout obscured
the response. These observations coexist.

78
00:05:36.154 --> 00:05:40.641
They do not prove that every boundary
independently caused the

79
00:05:40.641 --> 00:05:45.128
incident. Impact is one tenant, one
confirmed consequential transfer of

80
00:05:45.128 --> 00:05:49.615
100 synthetic fixture units, one missing
audit record, and one

81
00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:54.103
unverifiable notification. The three
action metrics are confirmed equals 1,

82
00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:58.590
missing equals 1, and unknown equals 1.
Duplicate writes after

83
00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:03.077
recovery equal 0. Compensation changes
operating from 900 back to

84
00:06:03.077 --> 00:06:07.564
1000 because 900 plus 100 equals 1000. It
changes reserve

85
00:06:07.564 --> 00:06:12.051
from 100 back to 0 because 100 minus 100

86
00:06:12.051 --> 00:06:16.538
equals 0. The visual classification is
transfer-100 under CONFIRMED, audit-7

87
00:06:16.538 --> 00:06:21.026
under MISSING, and notice-9 under UNKNOWN.
Only the missing action

88
00:06:21.026 --> 00:06:25.513
is eligible for a bounded idempotent
retry. The confirmed harmful

89
00:06:25.513 --> 00:06:30.000
action follows authorized compensation.
The unknown action stops and escalates.

90
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.375
The central rule is reconcile before
retry, rollback, replay, or

91
00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:38.750
acceptance. A transport timeout does not
prove that a write

92
00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:43.125
failed. Query the system of record with
the idempotency key

93
00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:47.500
or correlation identifier. Verify that the
binding still identifies the

94
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.875
same tenant, actor, action, and intended
postcondition. Then compare intended

95
00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:56.250
state with actual state. A confirmed and
acceptable action can

96
00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:00.625
be accepted. A confirmed but harmful
action can be compensated

97
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:05.000
only through a tested path with scoped
authorization and verification.

98
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.375
A missing action can be retried when the
failure is

99
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:13.750
transient and a retry budget remains. An
unauthorized, policy-blocked, or

100
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:18.125
deterministic validation failure must stop
and escalate rather than repeat

101
00:07:18.125 --> 00:07:22.500
unchanged. A pending or otherwise
unverifiable action remains UNKNOWN and

102
00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.875
also stops for escalation. In production,
a permitted transient retry

103
00:07:26.875 --> 00:07:31.250
would use provider guidance, exponential
backoff, jitter, idempotency, and a

104
00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:35.625
total budget. This local lab is
deterministic, so its single

105
00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:40.000
retry represents the decision that would
come before a production

106
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.375
delay schedule. Compensation is itself a
new consequential action. The

107
00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:48.750
approval for this lesson applies only to
the confirmed transfer

108
00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:53.125
identified in the fixture. It does not
authorize arbitrary transfers

109
00:07:53.125 --> 00:07:57.500
or a retry of the notification. A
successful command exit

110
00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:01.875
is not enough. Before closure, preserve
original evidence, prevent a

111
00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:06.250
second binding for the same idempotency
key, perform the required

112
00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:10.625
missing write, leave the unverifiable
action unresolved, and verify restored

113
00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:15.000
balances.

114
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.375
Here is a small demonstration before the
lab. Suppose a

115
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:23.750
notification request reaches its
destination, but the response times out.

116
00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:28.125
The responder pauses the send capability
and searches the operation

117
00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:32.500
ledger using the original identifiers. One
matching record exists, with

118
00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:36.875
the expected recipient and content
evidence. The destination read-back

119
00:08:36.875 --> 00:08:41.250
confirms one message. The correct
classification is CONFIRMED, so the

120
00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.625
responder does not retry. The missing
acknowledgment is recorded as

121
00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:50.000
a communication symptom, not as proof that
the message failed.

122
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.375
If the ledger contained no record, the
result would be

123
00:08:54.375 --> 00:08:58.750
MISSING only if the system of record were
authoritative and

124
00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:03.125
the query complete. If it contained a
pending record with

125
00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:07.500
no verified external postcondition, the
result would remain UNKNOWN. That

126
00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.875
action would be preserved and escalated,
not retried blindly. The

127
00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:16.250
same reasoning applies to transfer-100.
Its timeout describes the response

128
00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.625
path. L-1 and pay-100 describe the
persisted action. The latter

129
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:25.000
evidence controls recovery.

130
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.333
Pause and make your own reconciliation
table. For a timed-out

131
00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:33.667
consequential call, write what evidence
would distinguish completed, not

132
00:09:33.667 --> 00:09:38.000
completed, partial, conflicting, and
unknown outcomes. For each outcome, name

133
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:42.333
whether the next action is accept,
compensate, retry, rollback, or

134
00:09:42.333 --> 00:09:46.667
escalate. Include the identifier you would
query, the binding you

135
00:09:46.667 --> 00:09:51.000
would verify, and the postcondition you
would need.

136
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:25.500
Checkpoint. A write reached the server and
then timed out.

137
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.000
Should the workflow assume failure and
retry immediately?

138
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.545
The correct answer is no. A timeout
describes communication, not

139
00:12:34.545 --> 00:12:39.091
the final state of the external action.
Query the system

140
00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:43.636
of record with the operation key, verify
the target and

141
00:12:43.636 --> 00:12:48.182
intended postcondition, and then choose a
bounded action. If you

142
00:12:48.182 --> 00:12:52.727
chose immediate retry, add reconciliation
and idempotency first, because the

143
00:12:52.727 --> 00:12:57.273
original write may already exist. If you
chose never to

144
00:12:57.273 --> 00:13:01.818
retry, refine that rule. A proven
transient failure may be

145
00:13:01.818 --> 00:13:06.364
retried when the operation is idempotent,
the input is valid

146
00:13:06.364 --> 00:13:10.909
and authorized, provider guidance permits
it, and the total budget

147
00:13:10.909 --> 00:13:15.455
remains. The lesson is not never retry.
The lesson is

148
00:13:15.455 --> 00:13:20.000
never retry an uncertain consequential
action without evidence.

149
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.459
